@startuml edit-properties
|User|
start
:Select a component on the canvas or in the outline;
|Editor|
:Show its properties, in editor terms;
|User|
if (How is it changed?) then (properties panel)
  :Change a property;
elseif (How is it changed?) then (Enter, F2 or double-click)
  :Edit the label or value in place;
  if (Commit or cancel?) then (Esc)
    |Editor|
    :Restore the previous text;
    |User|
    stop
  else (Enter or leave the element)
  endif
else (Space on a checkbox or radio button)
  :Toggle its checked state;
endif
|Editor|
if (Editing imported formatted text?) then (yes)
  |User|
  if (Choose?) then (Keep formatting)
    :Edit with the formatting markup visible;
  else (Remove formatting)
    :Edit as literal text (undoable);
  endif
else (no)
endif
|Editor|
if (Can the change be written as valid source?) then (yes)
  if (Drop-down with options set to closed?) then (yes)
    :Remove the other options, with an
    undoable notice saying how many;
  else (no)
  endif
  :Update the canvas and the source;
  |Renderer|
  :Update the preview;
else (no)
  |Editor|
  :Do not offer the setting, or explain what is
  wrong; leave the component unchanged;
endif
|User|
stop
@enduml
